From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Topher Campbell <chrs2021@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 01/15] soc: mediatek: add MT6771 MCDI, SPM, SCP and LK framebuffer drivers

mtk-mcdi: keeps the SSPM's available-CPU mask in step with the online
CPUs and pauses MCDI (and cpuidle) across hotplug as MediaTek's kernel
does, and powers parked cores and empty clusters off through SiP calls.
Without it a core that enters PSCI power-down never wakes.

mt6771-spm: holds the AP's 26 MHz, bus and DRAM requests that the SPM
firmware holds on MediaTek's kernel (SPM_SRC_REQ 0x83), and optionally
(mt6771_spm.deep=1) starts the SPM firmware and suspends through it as
spm_go_to_sleep() does, refusing while a display, GPU or camera power
domain is still on; mt6771_spm.wake_mask sets the wake sources.

mt6771-scp: starts the SCP and talks to its sensor hub; the
accelerometer, gyroscope, magnetometer, light and proximity sensors
become IIO devices with several buffers each. The SCP's own sleep is off
by default; mt6771_scp.sleep=1 leaves it on, with the MT6358's sensor hub
supply mode and the SCP's clock mux on its request, as MediaTek's
scp_dvfs.c does.

mtk-lk-fb: hands the bootloader's live framebuffer to simplefb, for a
console before the display driver binds.
